{"crc":"9295d15b","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `FunctionTypeSerializer.serialize()` in `django/db/migrations/serializer.py`. When serializing a classmethod from a nested class, it uses `klass.__name__` which only gives the immediate class name (`Capability`), but it should use `klass.__qualname__` to get the full qualified name including the outer class (`Profile.Capability`).\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/migrations/serializer.py\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nclass FunctionTypeSerializer(BaseSerializer):\n    def serialize(self):\n        if getattr(self.value, \"__self__\", None) and isinstance(\n            self.value.__self__, type\n        ):\n            klass = self.value.__self__\n            module = klass.__module__\n            return \"%s.%s.%s\" % (module, klass.__name__, self.value.__name__), {\n                \"import %s\" % module\n            }\n=======\nclass FunctionTypeSerializer(BaseSerializer):\n    def serialize(self):\n        if getattr(self.value, \"__self__\", None) and isinstance(\n            self.value.__self__, type\n        ):\n            klass = self.value.__self__\n            module = klass.__module__\n            return \"%s.%s.%s\" % (module, klass.__qualname__, self.value.__name__), {\n                \"import %s\" % module\n            }\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQXH6YF5T94JWY589H3R1C0","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQXH6YA9TCB0XA70GFG33AY"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786435381.196188}
{"crc":"4e5f1887","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:8f881dae23ac141f63d606387f3d15834ab5481d8c22230e000c4afb2af10fe7","instance":"01KZQXH9YCZPWVYGJ3FJ074RGG","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `FunctionTypeSerializer.serialize()` in `django/db/migrations/serializer.py`. When serializing a classmethod from a nested class, it uses `klass.__name__` which only gives the immediate class name (`Capability`), but it should use `klass.__qualname__` to get the full qualified name including the outer class (`Profile.Capability`).\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/migrations/serializer.py\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nclass FunctionTypeSerializer(BaseSerializer):\n    def serialize(self):\n        if getattr(self.value, \"__self__\", None) and isinstance(\n            self.value.__self__, type\n        ):\n            klass = self.value.__self__\n            module = klass.__module__\n            return \"%s.%s.%s\" % (module, klass.__name__, self.value.__name__), {\n                \"import %s\" % module\n            }\n=======\nclass FunctionTypeSerializer(BaseSerializer):\n    def serialize(self):\n        if getattr(self.value, \"__self__\", None) and isinstance(\n            self.value.__self__, type\n        ):\n            klass = self.value.__self__\n            module = klass.__module__\n            return \"%s.%s.%s\" % (module, klass.__qualname__, self.value.__name__), {\n                \"import %s\" % module\n            }\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786435381.19633}
